        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-15T13:56:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, this is pretty involved. I\u0027m going to add some other folks, in case they have additional ideas - nothing immediately jumps out at me. I suspect that other clients will be okay - I don\u0027t think anyone but Chromium really uses SkPictureShader.",
      "parentUuid": "9227da15_c4ecec5f",
      "revId": "838ab27b0e937c5250cb707bc83f7d6d926de22c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb516e98_cab6c3a7",
        "filename": "src/shaders/SkPictureShader.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-15T14:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the picture shader has a local matrix applied, it seems like that gets respected AFTER rasterization happens? (Same is true in the GPU code path). In that situation, it seems like respecting the original surface props is going to create a bug -- you don\u0027t want to use LCD text unless the resulting image will be dropped to the final surface 1:1.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 308,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "838ab27b0e937c5250cb707bc83f7d6d926de22c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b15bfb5_ea247fdb",
        "filename": "src/shaders/SkPictureShader.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 10586
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-20T00:42:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rasterization happens in `SkPictureShader::rasterShader`, which looks like it already takes any scale/translation into account.  I guess there could be rotations, etc., that we\u0027d want to account for.\n\nI think the same also applies to the \"viewMatrix\" (the first param to `rasterShader`).\n\nI\u0027ve tweaked the logic in `SkPictureShader::rasterShader` and `SkPictureShader::asFragmentProcessor` to turn off LCDText in these cases.",
      "parentUuid": "fb516e98_cab6c3a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 308,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "838ab27b0e937c5250cb707bc83f7d6d926de22c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa06d9d1_d88bb3df",
        "filename": "src/shaders/SkPictureShader.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-20T13:26:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My intuition (but I\u0027m still not 100% on how this all works) was: The view matrix (and aspects of the local matrix) are used to determine the size of the offscreen surface. However, the resulting offscreen image is then drawn like a normal image shader. If that image shader has any transformation beyond integer translation, then LCD text is going to be wrong. The local matrix (but not the view matrix?) is applied to the image, AFTER its rasterized.\n\nIn other words: If you make a picture shader from a picture, and specify a 90 degree rotation in the local matrix ... we\u0027ll render the context in the original orientation, then rotate the resulting image as we draw it to the final surface. Similarly if the local matrix has a half-pixel translation. If I\u0027m right about those cases, then I think that the local matrix has to be restricted to integer translation or we want to turn off LCD.\n\nAnd I\u0027m still not positive about how the view matrix is applied, because the way that it\u0027s plumbed and used in the cached image info struct isn\u0027t entirely clear - the matrix that\u0027s actually applied at draw time (of the picture) is just a rect-to-rect matrix based on the bounds of the picture and tile?",
      "parentUuid": "7b15bfb5_ea247fdb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 308,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "838ab27b0e937c5250cb707bc83f7d6d926de22c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
