      "writtenOn": "2022-07-20T13:26:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right - it just stores a pixmap (same as RP blitter). I think you\u0027ll need to plumb the surface props in (like you did for RP blitter) - I tagged the two spots in SkBlitter.cpp where the VM blitters are created (it\u0027s right next to the RP blitter creation).\n\nUltimately, certain SkPaints can only be drawn using the VM blitter, so we really need both of them to have the same functionality in this regard (or it\u0027s going to produce some surprising results).\n\nHowever, I agree that we can do the VM one separately - it\u0027s going to be complex on its own (there is caching logic in the VM blitter construction that needs to account for this).",
      "parentUuid": "2164b81b_2d157168",
